# The finite-sequence verifier returns two outer bound-check Results, three
# named WD Results, and a local index scope containing both the N+ parameter
# FactId and the retained `index <= 3` domain FactId. The compiler pushes that
# exact Result scope, compiles the return check, pops it, then publishes the
# finite-sequence membership, function membership, and defining equality.
have finite_seq bounded_sequence finite_seq(R, 3) for index <= 3, bounded_sequence(index) = index + 1
bounded_sequence(2) = 2 + 1
